# It begins

Tomorrow I start the [Te Araroa Trail](http://teararoa.org.nz/) which is a massive walk from one end of Aotearoa New Zealand to the other. That's over 3,000 kilometres and will probably take many months.

## Why?

Honestly I don't have a great reason but I think the only time I've been properly happy has been when out and about  in nature, so when I left my job I didn't have anything specific to do but really didn't want to grouse around at home for a while. Instead this seems like a great opportunity to enjoy the beautiful NZ summer and make my way through the cultural and natural experiences of this country.

## How?

I've flown north and taken the bus further north and will get the shuttle even further north. From there I will mostly walk south over and over until eventually reaching Bluff at the very south. The exact details I don't know but I'll have to work it out along the way. There's quite a lot of logistics to manage with washing clothes, food, water, gas, etc. I have a tent for sleeping in and associated paraphernalia for sleeping out in the wild.

## Other thoughts 

I hope it'll be fun and I meet awesome people along the way. I have a bunch of goals but I want to expound on those in subsequent posts. I also want to post a vlog per day of walking. There's not much point in a vlog when I'm just staying in a town though. There is always the possibility of giving up or failing at some point but hopefully if that happens, it occurs safely.